      "f": "Solid state drive",
      "g": "A1.1",
      "ib": "A secondary storage device that stores data in non-volatile flash memory chips and has no moving parts.",
      "q": "Explain why SSDs are used in most laptops. [3]",
      "a": [
        "They have no moving parts, so they are more robust when the laptop is moved or knocked;",
        "they have faster read/write speeds, so the laptop boots and loads programs faster;",
        "they are lighter and use less power, improving battery life."
      ],
      "h": 0,
