      "g": "A3.2",
      "ib": "Deliberately adding redundant data back into a normalised database, for example by merging tables, to improve the speed of read queries at the cost of extra storage and a greater risk of inconsistency.",
      "q": "Evaluate the decision to denormalise a database used to produce weekly sales reports. [4]",
