      "f": "",
      "g": "A1.3",
      "ib": "A conflict that occurs when two or more processes need the same resource (CPU time, memory, a file, a printer) at the same time, so the OS must decide who gets it and the others must wait.",
      "q": "Describe how an operating system manages resource contention. [3]",
      "a": [
        "When several processes request the same resource, the OS grants it to one and queues the others.",
        "It uses mutual exclusion (locks or semaphores) so only one process can use a non-shareable resource at a time.",
        "It orders the waiting processes using priorities and scheduling, and ageing so that none starves."
      ],
      "h": 1,
