      "g": "A3.4",
      "ib": "Storing copies of the same data on more than one node of a distributed database, to improve availability, fault tolerance and read speed; the copies must be kept consistent when data changes.",
      "q": "Explain one benefit and one drawback of replication. [2]",
      "a": [
        "Benefit: if one node fails, the data is still available from another copy, and reads can be served from the nearest node;",
        "drawback: every update must be applied to all copies, which uses bandwidth and can leave copies briefly inconsistent."
      ],
