      "q": "Explain how recursion solves a problem. [3]",
      "a": [
        "The function breaks the problem into a smaller version of the same problem and calls itself to solve it (the recursive case).",
        "Each call works on a smaller input, moving towards the base case.",
        "The base case is solved directly; its result is returned to the call before, and the results are combined as the calls return (unwind) to give the final answer."
      ],
      "h": 1,
