      "f": "",
      "g": "CS",
      "ib": "A generative model that is trained by adding random noise to images step by step and learning to remove it; to generate, it starts from pure random noise and removes the predicted noise over many steps until an image remains.",
      "q": "Outline how a diffusion model generates an image. [3]",
      "a": [
        "Generation starts from an image of pure random noise.",
        "At each step a trained neural network (usually a CNN such as a U-Net) predicts the noise in the image, and some of it is removed.",
        "After many steps (sampling steps) a clear image is left; a text prompt can steer (condition) every step towards the requested content."
      ],
      "h": 0,
      "p": "Case-study",
      "s": "diffusion",
