      "f": "",
      "g": "A2.4",
      "ib": "Giving each user, program or process only the minimum access rights it needs to do its job, so that a mistake or a compromised account can do as little damage as possible.",
      "q": "Explain how the principle of least privilege improves the security of a school network. [2]",
      "a": [
        "Each account gets only the permissions it needs (students cannot open staff or admin areas);",
        "so if one account is compromised, the attacker can reach far less data and fewer systems."
      ],
