      "s": "binary",
      "h": 0,
      "m": 3,
      "q": "Determine the hexadecimal value of the binary number 11010111, and explain why programmers use hexadecimal.",
      "a": [
        "1101 = D and 0111 = 7, so D7;",
        "hexadecimal is shorter and easier for humans to read and remember than binary;",
        "and it converts easily to and from binary (one hex digit = four bits), so fewer mistakes are made."
      ],
      "c": "Determine",
      "id": "2d830b7e2",
      "u": "A1",
      "n": "A1-data-logic.binary",
      "f": "easi|hexadecimal|hex"
