      "p": "A1-data-logic",
      "s": "binary",
      "h": 0,
      "m": 2,
      "q": "Outline why hexadecimal is used by programmers.",
      "a": [
        "Each hex digit stands for exactly 4 bits, so it converts to and from binary easily;",
        "it is shorter and easier for humans to read, write and remember than long binary strings, so there are fewer mistakes (e.g. colour codes, MAC addresses, memory addresses)."
      ],
      "c": "Outline",
