      "s": "kmap",
      "h": 0,
      "m": 3,
      "q": "Outline how a Karnaugh map is used to simplify a Boolean expression.",
      "a": [
        "The outputs from the truth table are placed in a grid in Gray code order, so adjacent cells differ by one variable;",
        "adjacent 1s are grouped into rectangles of 1, 2, 4 or 8 cells, as large as possible (groups may wrap around the edges);",
        "each group gives one term containing only the variables that do not change within it, and the terms are combined with OR."
      ],
      "c": "Outline",
      "id": "c9e5e6e08",
      "u": "A1",
      "n": "A1-data-logic.kmap",
      "f": "karnaugh map",
