      "h": 0,
      "m": 2,
      "q": "Explain why a stack is a suitable data structure for an “undo” feature in a text editor.",
      "a": [
        "Each action is pushed onto the stack as it is performed, so the most recent action is always at the top;",
        "undo pops the top action, reversing the most recent change first, which matches the LIFO order of a stack."
      ],
      "c": "Explain",
      "id": "f32357d32",
      "u": "B2",
      "n": "B2-data-structures.stacks",
      "f": "data structure",
