      "h": 0,
      "m": 2,
      "q": "Explain why a queue is used to hold documents waiting to be printed.",
      "a": [
        "Documents should be printed in the order in which they were sent;",
        "a queue adds each new document at the rear and removes the next one to print from the front, so the first sent is printed first (FIFO)."
      ],
      "c": "Explain",
      "id": "3f0a2d94d",
      "u": "B2",
      "n": "B2-data-structures.queues",
      "f": "remov|rear|document"
