      "h": 0,
      "m": 2,
      "q": "Distinguish between a for loop and a while loop.",
      "a": [
        "A for loop is a counted loop that repeats a known number of times, e.g. once for each item in a list or range;",
        "whereas a while loop is a conditional loop that repeats for as long as a condition is true, when the number of repetitions is not known in advance."
      ],
      "c": "Distinguish",
