      "h": 0,
      "m": 3,
      "q": "State the time complexity of linear search and binary search, and explain which scales better to large data sets.",
      "a": [
        "Linear search is O(n);",
        "binary search is O(log n);",
        "binary search scales better: doubling the data adds only one extra comparison, whereas for linear search the number of comparisons doubles."
      ],
      "c": "State",
      "id": "75efb791e",
      "u": "B2",
      "n": "B2-algorithms.bigo",
      "f": "time complexity|linear search|binary search",
