      "p": "B2-algorithms",
      "s": "search",
      "h": 0,
      "m": 3,
      "q": "Justify the use of a binary search rather than a linear search to find a student’s record in a list of 1500 records sorted by student ID.",
      "a": [
        "The list is already sorted by ID, which binary search requires.",
        "Binary search halves the remaining records with each comparison, so it is O(log n): at most 11 comparisons for 1500 records (2<sup>11</sup> = 2048).",
        "Linear search is O(n) and could need all 1500 comparisons, so binary search is much faster, especially as records are looked up often."
      ],
