      "s": "static",
      "h": 0,
      "m": 2,
      "q": "Distinguish between a static method and an instance (non-static) method.",
      "a": [
        "A static method belongs to the class and is called through the class name; it has no self, so it cannot use any object’s instance attributes;",
        "an instance method is called on a particular object and receives that object as self, so it can read and change that object’s own attributes."
      ],
      "c": "Distinguish",
