      "h": 0,
      "m": 3,
      "q": "Explain how encapsulation can protect the balance of a bank account object.",
      "a": [
        "The balance attribute is made private, so code outside the class cannot change it directly;",
        "it can only be changed through public methods such as deposit() and withdraw();",
        "these methods validate each change, e.g. rejecting negative deposits or withdrawals larger than the balance, so the balance always stays valid."
      ],
      "c": "Explain",
