      "s": "encapsulation",
      "h": 0,
      "m": 4,
      "q": "Explain two benefits of encapsulation.",
      "a": [
        "Data is protected: attributes are private and can only be changed through methods…",
        "…which can validate new values, so an object can never be put into an invalid state (e.g. a negative balance).",
        "The internal implementation is hidden behind a public interface…",
        "…so it can be changed or improved later without changing any of the code that uses the class, making maintenance easier."
      ],
      "c": "Explain",
