      "s": "cpu",
      "h": 0,
      "m": 3,
      "q": "Explain why a quad-core processor may not run a program four times faster than a single-core processor.",
      "a": [
        "The program may not be designed to be split into parallel tasks, or some parts must run in sequence;",
        "the cores must coordinate and share resources such as cache, RAM and buses, which adds overhead;",
        "so some cores sit idle or wait, and the speed-up is less than four times."
      ],
      "t": "core",
      "c": "Explain",
      "id": "e9641df59",
