      "p": "A4-data",
      "s": "cleaning",
      "h": 1,
      "m": 3,
      "q": "Compare deletion and imputation as ways of handling missing data.",
      "a": [
        "Both deal with values missing from a data set before training.",
        "Deletion removes the incomplete rows (or features); it is simple but loses data and can bias the sample if values are missing for a reason.",
        "Imputation fills the gaps with estimates such as the mean or a predicted value; it keeps all the records but the estimates may not be accurate."
      ],
      "t": "imputation",
      "c": "Compare",
      "id": "908c8278b",
      "u": "A4",
