      "s": "classify",
      "h": 1,
      "m": 3,
      "q": "Explain why decision trees are often used for medical diagnosis.",
      "a": [
        "A decision tree classifies a patient by following a series of tests on features such as symptoms and test results until it reaches a diagnosis (a leaf).",
        "Its decisions are transparent: a doctor can follow and check every step of the reasoning,",
        "which matters for accountability and trust in medicine, and it works with fairly small data sets."
      ],
      "t": "decision-tree",
      "c": "Explain",
      "id": "c06481390",
